STAFF ID CARD DESK

Staff Id Card Desk — a real-world task using only today's concepts: defining a function with def, parameters, calling a function, writing it once and reusing it, upper(), while validation, comparisons, if / else, variables, input(), and printing. No imports, no tricks.

Solve it individually, then come together as a group to compare approaches. Good luck!

A new guest house on Stadium Road prints staff ID cards every time it hires. The manager wants a program where the card is printed by ONE function - written once, then called for every new staff member. Typing the card lines three times by hand is exactly what functions exist to end.

The program must:
- Contain a function that takes a name and a department and prints the card:
  ----- STAFF CARD -----
  NAME: ADAEZE OBI
  DEPT: ACCOUNTS
  VALID: 2026/27
  ----------------------
  (name and department in ALL CAPS; VALID is always 2026/27)
- Ask "How many new staff: " (at least 1), then for each one ask the name and department, and print the card by CALLING the function - the card lines appear nowhere else in the program.
- After the last card: NEW STAFF PRINTED: 3

Sample run:

How many new staff: 2
Staff 1 name: Adaeze Obi
Staff 1 department: Accounts
----- STAFF CARD -----
NAME: ADAEZE OBI
DEPT: ACCOUNTS
VALID: 2026/27
----------------------
Staff 2 name: Emeka Woke
Staff 2 department: Security
----- STAFF CARD -----
NAME: EMEKA WOKE
DEPT: SECURITY
VALID: 2026/27
----------------------
NEW STAFF PRINTED: 2

Edge cases to handle: one staff member only, a department typed with lowercase (card shows caps), a two-word department like Front Desk, and - the real test of the day - a friend reading your code should find the card printed in exactly ONE place, with the function called once per staff member.
